  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#2837', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''believ'':77 ''could'':66 ''d'':39 ''day'':47 ''die'':93 ''fact'':49 ''faith'':4,86 ''fear'':10 ''focus'':20 ''generat'':97 ''giant'':25 ''go'':40 ''gone'':52 ''got'':60 ''gotten'':68 ''grape'':22 ''grate'':33 ''instead'':23,28,87 ''isn'':98 ''israel'':69 ''like'':36 ''m'':32 ''mani'':56 ''oh'':95 ''optim'':14 ''peopl'':18,35 ''pessim'':17 ''pomegran'':27 ''principl'':94 ''problem'':30 ''rather'':5,15 ''readi'':100 ''share'':79 ''simpli'':75 ''spirit'':2,8,12,82 ''trek'':43,54 ''wonder'':91,92'::tsvector, '{"text":"A spirit of faith rather than a spirit of fear, a spirit of optimism rather than pessimism? People that focus on grapes instead of giants, and pomegranates instead of problems. I''m grateful for people like that. I''d go on a trek with them any day. In fact, I have gone on trek with many of them. They got me through it, and they could have gotten Israel through it too if they simply had believed and shared in that spirit and in that faith. Instead, here''s the wonder, wonder, die principle. Oh, that generation isn''t ready.","seq_end":2847,"t_end_s":11243.825,"seq_start":2837,"t_start_s":11207.49,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#2894', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''12'':83 ''adulteri'':34 ''back'':86 ''bear'':28 ''breach'':10 ''bring'':48,54 ''broke'':14 ''cannot'':47 ''cheat'':41 ''children'':26 ''choic'':79 ''come'':85 ''concern'':103 ''could'':19 ''coven'':37 ''faith'':62 ''get'':21 ''giant'':99 ''grape'':90 ''great'':70 ''infidel'':32 ''know'':8 ''land'':24 ''ll'':7,53 ''long'':58 ''make'':81 ''oh'':95 ''pomegran'':94 ''promis'':12,16,23 ''put'':4 ''re'':61 ''see'':64 ''spi'':84 ''tragedi'':71 ''ve'':39 ''way'':2 ''whoredom'':30'::tsvector, '{"text":"The way he puts it, you''ll know my breach of promise. You broke your promise, so you could not get the promised land. Your children will bear your whoredoms, your infidelities, your adultery against the covenant. You''ve been cheating on me, and so I cannot bring you in. But I''ll bring them in as long as they''re faithful. You see, that to me is the great tragedy of all of this. They had a choice to make. The 12 spies come back. Here''s the grapes. Here''s the pomegranates. Oh, here''s the giants. Here''s the concerns.","seq_end":2904,"t_end_s":11478.91,"seq_start":2894,"t_start_s":11442.189,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#2905', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''10'':17 ''alreadi'':126 ''although'':81 ''back'':106 ''believ'':2 ''cross'':114 ''die'':41,43 ''even'':103 ''faith'':21 ''fear'':14 ''generat'':51 ''go'':98 ''god'':4,33,67,84,118 ''ironi'':57 ''israel'':11 ''late'':124 ''lesser'':29 ''let'':34,37 ''ll'':97 ''made'':127 ''mind'':91,130 ''moment'':62 ''natur'':30 ''never'':90 ''new'':50 ''okay'':95 ''part'':79 ''probabl'':82 ''re'':111 ''readi'':112 ''realiz'':64 ''remors'':76 ''river'':116 ''sad'':10 ''said'':109 ''serious'':75 ''sorri'':101 ''sorrow'':80,85 ''succumb'':26 ''take'':105 ''told'':70 ''trust'':12 ''two'':24 ''us'':8 ''wait'':47 ''wander'':39,40,42'::tsvector, '{"text":"But believe, and God will be with us. And sadly, Israel trusted the fear of the 10 more than the faith of the two and succumbed to their lesser natures. And so God let them. And let them wander, wander, die, wander, die because I can wait for a new generation. And so he does. The irony there is in that moment of realization of what God has just told them, there''s some serious remorse on their part. Sorrow, although probably not godly sorrow. Just, no, no, no. Never mind then. It''s okay. We''ll go. We we sorry. We even we take back what we said. We''re ready to cross the river, and God is, no. It''s too late. You already made up your mind.","seq_end":2914,"t_end_s":11527.414,"seq_start":2905,"t_start_s":11479.63,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#2932', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''44'':39 ''alway'':7 ''amalekit'':81 ''ark'':57 ''back'':119,134 ''book'':107 ''came'':82 ''camp'':71 ''canaanit'':86 ''coven'':60 ''depart'':66 ''discomfort'':96 ''dwelt'':88 ''eat'':27 ''even'':98 ''expens'':153 ''faith'':155 ''fear'':150 ''forward'':123,126 ''giant'':24 ''go'':43,125 ''god'':54,117,137 ''gonna'':52 ''good'':16 ''hearken'':115 ''hill'':91 ''hilltop'':47 ''hormon'':100 ''idea'':17 ''ll'':6 ''lord'':63 ''mose'':65 ''murmur'':135 ''nevertheless'':55 ''number'':109 ''nutshel'':112 ''obey'':53 ''okay'':72 ''one'':3 ''onto'':45 ''presum'':41 ''prophet'':140 ''re'':49,74 ''realli'':25 ''say'':2 ''smote'':93 ''spit'':31 ''stay'':118,133 ''still'':50 ''suffer'':148 ''tell'':130 ''thing'':144 ''unto'':99 ''vers'':38 ''want'':141 ''way'':103,147 ''went'':122 ''whole'':106'::tsvector, '{"text":"He says one, and you''ll always do the other. So this is not a good idea. He''s not with you. Those giants really will eat you up and spit you out. And so they did. Verse 44, they presumed to go up onto the hilltop. They''re still not gonna obey God. Nevertheless, the ark of the covenant of the Lord and Moses departed not out of the camp. Okay. You''re on your own then. Then the Amalekites came down and the Canaanites which dwelt in that hill and smote them and discomforted them even unto Hormon. In a way, is the whole book of Numbers in a nutshell, of not hearkening to God, staying back when he went forward or going forward when he''s telling them to stay back, murmuring against God and his prophets, wanting to do things their own way, suffering through fear at the expense of faith,","seq_end":2942,"t_end_s":11654.91,"seq_start":2932,"t_start_s":11602.135,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#3157', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''alreadi'':72 ''ambit'':47 ''avaric'':40 ''blame'':51,86 ''brought'':94 ''d'':71 ''decept'':81 ''dominion'':46 ''done'':66,103 ''excus'':43 ''failur'':55 ''faith'':27 ''fear'':31 ''go'':25,35 ''gone'':5 ''greed'':38 ''haven'':2 ''honey'':12 ''insidi'':78 ''land'':8,60 ''lead'':83 ''milk'':10 ''other'':87 ''promis'':59 ''re'':34 ''reach'':57 ''righteous'':42 ''self'':80 ''someth'':77 ''thing'':91,100 ''unright'':45 ''upon'':95 ''us'':16,52,84 ''vaniti'':48 ''ve'':93,102 ''way'':69 ''went'':29 ''would'':64 ''wouldn'':23'::tsvector, '{"text":"Why haven''t we gone into the land of milk and honey? It''s not us. That''s on you because you wouldn''t go with faith. You went with fear. Now you''re going with with greed and avarice and righteous, excuse me, unrighteous dominion, ambition, vanity. Do not blame us for your failure to reach the promised land, because if you would have done it our way, we''d already be there. There''s something insidious about self deception. It leads us to blame others for the very things we''ve brought upon ourselves or the very things we''ve done to them.","seq_end":3170,"t_end_s":12580.025,"seq_start":3157,"t_start_s":12538.38,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#3556', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''beg'':22 ''bring'':13 ''brought'':70 ''come'':8 ''d'':20 ''deliver'':24 ''drink'':49 ''eclips'':76 ''egypt'':11,26 ''evil'':17 ''faith'':78 ''fear'':75 ''fig'':37,66 ''forward'':84 ''interest'':87 ''israelit'':90 ''jordan'':61 ''look'':92 ''made'':5 ''misplac'':97 ''move'':83 ''neither'':43 ''nostalgia'':98 ''past'':95 ''place'':18,32 ''pomegran'':42,68 ''proof'':72 ''say'':28 ''seed'':34 ''side'':58 ''us'':6,14 ''vine'':39 ''water'':47 ''well'':50 ''wherefor'':2 ''wouldn'':81 ''yeah'':51'::tsvector, '{"text":"And wherefore have you made us to come out of Egypt to bring us into this evil place? You''d been begging for deliverance in Egypt. They say, it''s no place of seed or of figs or vines or of pomegranates, neither is there any water to drink. Well, yeah, because it''s on the other side of the Jordan. There I there were figs and pomegranates. I brought you proof. But your fear eclipsed your faith, and you wouldn''t move forward. It''s interesting that these Israelites are looking at their past with misplaced nostalgia.","seq_end":3566,"t_end_s":14163.85,"seq_start":3556,"t_start_s":14128.045,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#3583', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''10'':86 ''aaron'':89 ''alway'':51 ''around'':39 ''ask'':12,22,32,73 ''build'':65 ''chanc'':63 ''complain'':40 ''congreg'':92 ''exercis'':46 ''faith'':30,48 ''far'':98 ''fight'':18 ''flow'':81 ''forth'':82 ''freeli'':83 ''gather'':90 ''give'':60 ''go'':38 ''good'':100 ''hear'':128 ''kind'':4 ''m'':57 ''mose'':87,126 ''need'':25,77 ''oh'':108 ''pray'':23 ''problem'':54 ''re'':110,118 ''rebel'':131 ''rock'':72,96,124 ''said'':103 ''say'':127 ''simpli'':68 ''sometim'':7 ''speak'':69,114,121 ''suppos'':112,119 ''thing'':20 ''togeth'':93 ''tri'':58 ''uh'':107 ''uh-oh'':106 ''unto'':104 ''vers'':85 ''water'':26 ''well'':84 ''ye'':130'::tsvector, '{"text":"And with this kind that''s sometimes all you have to ask. You don''t have to fight for things. Just ask. Pray. You need water? Then have the faith to ask me for it. Don''t go around complaining that it''s not there. Exercise your faith. That''s always been the problem here. I''m trying to give you a chance to build it. So simply speak to the rock. Ask for what you need and it will flow forth freely. Well, verse 10, Moses and Aaron gathered the congregation together before the rock. So far so good. And he said unto them, uh-oh, you''re not supposed to speak to them. You''re supposed to speak to the rock. But Moses says, hear now ye rebels.","seq_end":3593,"t_end_s":14290.005,"seq_start":3583,"t_start_s":14249.09,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#3842', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''accord'':90 ''alma'':66 ''beauti'':62,81 ''book'':93 ''brazen'':7 ''come'':21 ''contrit'':49 ''doesn'':85,97 ''etern'':59 ''even'':12,33,53 ''explain'':99 ''faith'':46 ''god'':44 ''later'':70 ''least'':88 ''life'':56 ''lift'':4,17 ''live'':32,52 ''look'':27,39 ''mani'':24,36 ''might'':51 ''mose'':84,96 ''nephi'':64,68,71 ''number'':95 ''peopl'':75 ''serpent'':8,30 ''shall'':14 ''son'':42 ''spirit'':50 ''stori'':82 ''teach'':73,77 ''unto'':54 ''upon'':28,40 ''us'':78 ''wilder'':11'::tsvector, '{"text":"And as he lifted up the brazen serpent in the wilderness, even so shall he be lifted up who should come. And as many as should look upon that serpent should live. Even so as many as should look upon the son of God with faith, having a contrite spirit might live even unto that life which is eternal. That''s beautiful what Nephi and Alma and Nephi, the later Nephi, are teaching their people and teaching us about this beautiful story. Because Moses doesn''t at least not according to the book of Numbers, Moses doesn''t explain what this is all about.","seq_end":3847,"t_end_s":15320.44,"seq_start":3842,"t_start_s":15286.105,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#3869', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''believ'':25 ''contrit'':7 ''day'':54 ''earth'':38 ''evil'':105 ''faith'':3 ''famili'':45 ''get'':75 ''go'':41,59 ''god'':14 ''got'':62 ''great'':64 ''high'':107 ''idea'':65 ''know'':74 ''lack'':2,5 ''like'':35,97 ''look'':29 ''m'':99 ''mayb'':77 ''might'':19,31 ''monday'':80 ''night'':81 ''nonsens'':21 ''oh'':60 ''onslaught'':48 ''pictur'':56 ''place'':108 ''power'':103 ''prophet'':58 ''protect'':43 ''re'':96 ''realli'':12 ''say'':69 ''share'':87 ''sing'':83 ''song'':85 ''sound'':20,32 ''spirit'':8 ''stori'':89 ''togeth'':76 ''treat'':93 ''wicked'':51 ''world'':50 ''yeah'':17'::tsvector, '{"text":"They lacked faith. They lacked a contrite spirit. And that''s really what God is after. Yeah. This might sound nonsensical. Will you just believe? Will you just look? This might sound it''s like how on earth are we going to protect our families from the onslaught of worldly wickedness in our day? You picture the prophets going, Oh, I got a great idea. What do you say we, I don''t know, get together maybe on a Monday night and sing some songs and share some stories and have some treats? And we''re like, I''m up against the powers of evil in high places.","seq_end":3882,"t_end_s":15464.6,"seq_start":3869,"t_start_s":15425.075,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#3883', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''amaz'':10 ''away'':89 ''back'':53 ''belli'':106 ''bitter'':101 ''caus'':68 ''d'':8 ''enough'':26 ''even'':52 ''exercis'':20 ''faith'':22 ''game'':5 ''give'':16 ''good'':50 ''humbl'':25 ''idea'':56 ''israel'':46 ''let'':99 ''live'':14 ''ll'':30 ''look'':12,59 ''lord'':34 ''make'':75 ''matter'':83 ''mayb'':72,79 ''point'':77 ''problem'':71 ''quit'':85 ''run'':88 ''see'':108 ''serpent'':62,65 ''settl'':103 ''shot'':19 ''sin'':92 ''sit'':93 ''song'':2 ''spirit'':27 ''swell'':111 ''tri'':86 ''water'':102 ''way'':36,40,113 ''work'':42 ''yeah'':6,47'::tsvector, '{"text":"A song and a game? Yeah. You''d be amazed. Just look and live. Just give it a shot. Exercise some faith. Have a humble enough spirit that you''ll do it the Lord''s way. How''s your way been working out for you, Israel? Yeah. Not so good. But even back to that idea of why look at a serpent when a serpent was the cause of my problems, maybe he''s making a point there. Maybe it''s a matter of quit trying to run away from your sins. Sit with them for a while. Let this bitter water settle into your belly and see if it swells the way it should.","seq_end":3893,"t_end_s":15506.095,"seq_start":3883,"t_start_s":15465.319,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#4401', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''accept'':61 ''afford'':13 ''balaam'':16,48,97 ''balak'':72 ''believ'':85 ''destruct'':82 ''didn'':59 ''differ'':102 ''ear'':26 ''end'':40,99 ''error'':51 ''eye'':22 ''faith'':36 ''forward'':34 ''god'':66,86 ''hear'':28 ''honor'':74 ''least'':47 ''left'':57 ''merci'':95 ''might'':43 ''move'':33 ''need'':5,19 ''okay'':45 ''path'':103 ''prepar'':8 ''saw'':49 ''see'':24 ''self'':81 ''sometim'':88 ''suggest'':100 ''think'':44 ''treasur'':65 ''us'':92 ''way'':54 ''willing'':31 ''withheld'':67,76'::tsvector, '{"text":"That''s what we need to be preparing for. We can''t afford to be Balaam''s. We need to have eyes to see and ears to hear, and the willingness to move forward in faith. Now if we ended there, we might think, okay, at least Balaam saw the error of his ways and he left and didn''t accept all of their treasures, God withheld him not only from Balak''s honor, but withheld him from his own self destruction. I do believe God does sometimes do that with us in his mercy. But Balaam''s end suggests a different path for him.","seq_end":4414,"t_end_s":17708.256,"seq_start":4401,"t_start_s":17670.781,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#4693', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''000'':10 ''2'':9 ''601'':4 ''730'':5 ''actual'':62 ''almost'':34 ''anoth'':14 ''anyway'':93 ''arm'':88 ''bigger'':71 ''conquer'':65 ''could'':78 ''differ'':11 ''faith'':105 ''far'':41,46 ''firstborn'':29 ''flesh'':90 ''go'':63 ''group'':59,74,102 ''hous'':37 ''ident'':36 ''israel'':39 ''land'':68 ''less'':7 ''levit'':26 ''like'':19 ''matter'':92 ''miracl'':18 ''never'':83,87 ''number'':24,53,84 ''one'':15,31 ''parent'':108 ''physic'':49 ''promis'':67 ''question'':96 ''real'':95 ''saw'':21 ''say'':57 ''size'':44 ''spiritu'':98 ''strength'':50,51'::tsvector, '{"text":"Now there''s 601,730. So less than 2,000 difference. That''s another one of those miracles like we saw with the numbering the Levites and the firstborn. This one, it''s almost an identical house of Israel as far as its size, as far as its physical strength, strength in numbers, if you can say, the group that''s actually going to conquer the promised land was no bigger than the group before them that could have because it was never numbers. It was never arm of flesh that mattered anyway. The real question is spiritual. And will this group be more faithful than their parents?","seq_end":4704,"t_end_s":18757.27,"seq_start":4693,"t_start_s":18713.36,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#4714', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''27'':74 ''ago'':89 ''brother'':100 ''chapter'':73 ''come'':102 ''complet'':22 ''conquer'':61 ''daughter'':82,94 ''experi'':7 ''faith'':34 ''fear'':38 ''follow'':71 ''forward'':103 ''generat'':44,54 ''gentl'':15 ''god'':72 ''honest'':48 ''land'':64 ''mention'':80 ''moment'':88 ''mose'':110 ''outliv'':37 ''personifi'':46 ''promis'':63 ''question'':108 ''readi'':59,65,69 ''realli'':35 ''redeem'':67 ''replac'':23 ''rock'':10 ''saw'':3 ''second'':28 ''see'':32,77 ''smite'':8 ''spoken'':16 ''take'':29 ''total'':27 ''two'':92 ''vers'':91 ''wait'':51 ''well'':39 ''zelaphat'':84,96 ''zion'':68'::tsvector, '{"text":"And we saw why in this experience, smiting the rock when he should have gently spoken to it. This is a complete replacement. This is a total second take. And to see if faith really does outlive fear, well, here you have a generation to personify it. Honestly, I am waiting for a generation to do just that. Ready to conquer the Promised Land? Ready to redeem Zion? Ready to follow God? Chapter 27, now we see why we mentioned the daughters of Zelaphat just a few moments ago. In verse two, the daughters of Zelaphat, they have no brothers, they come forward and they have a question for Moses.","seq_end":4727,"t_end_s":18837.455,"seq_start":4714,"t_start_s":18794.11,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#4928', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''come'':65 ''commit'':28,74 ''daughter'':14 ''experi'':59 ''faith'':21 ''femal'':39 ''field'':33 ''gender'':43 ''get'':40 ''great'':103 ''help'':94 ''idea'':104 ''insight'':61 ''issu'':44 ''lot'':57 ''m'':76,86 ''make'':77 ''male'':38 ''mentor'':53 ''might'':36 ''mission'':32 ''moment'':7 ''okay'':46 ''past'':41 ''person'':73 ''plan'':83 ''pleas'':47 ''re'':4 ''repent'':25 ''say'':98 ''set'':87 ''someon'':17,54 ''spiritu'':52 ''think'':10,49 ''vow'':80 ''weigh'':69 ''whatev'':34 ''wisdom'':62 ''would'':91 ''yeah'':99 ''young'':13,18,23,26,29'::tsvector, '{"text":"And if you''re in a moment of again, think of a young daughter here, just someone young in the faith or young in repentance, young in commitment, young in the mission field, whatever it might be, male, female, get past the gender issues here. Okay? Please. And think if a spiritual mentor, someone with a lot more experience and insight, wisdom were to come to me and weigh in on the personal commitment I''m making and the vow or the plan that I''m setting out for myself, would it be helpful for them to say, Yeah, that''s a great idea.","seq_end":4937,"t_end_s":19600.014,"seq_start":4928,"t_start_s":19562.105,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#4963', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''actual'':43 ''begin'':63 ''bond'':22 ''bound'':26 ''chapter'':66 ''convers'':85 ''day'':10 ''disallow'':6,39 ''faith'':82 ''five'':3 ''forgiv'':35 ''gave'':55 ''god'':41 ''hath'':25 ''hear'':106 ''heareth'':13 ''keep'':68 ''know'':105 ''like'':51 ''lord'':33 ''made'':71 ''merci'':47 ''might'':92 ''oath'':73 ''older'':96 ''person'':99 ''promis'':53 ''repent'':88 ''saw'':60 ''say'':103 ''shall'':29,34 ''soul'':28 ''stand'':30 ''step'':100 ''tri'':44 ''vers'':2 ''vow'':18 ''whatev'':90 ''wherewith'':23 ''wiser'':98 ''word'':57 ''young'':79'::tsvector, '{"text":"But verse five, if he disallow her in the day that he heareth, not any of her vows or of her bonds wherewith she hath bound her soul shall stand. And the Lord shall forgive her because he disallowed her. God''s actually trying to be merciful here. It''s like you promised, you gave your word, and we saw at the beginning of this chapter, you keep it, you made the oath. But again, if we are young in our faith or our conversion or our repentance or whatever it might be, if a older or wiser person steps in and says, you know what?","seq_end":4968,"t_end_s":19741.32,"seq_start":4963,"t_start_s":19708.805,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#5135', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''40'':79 ''anoth'':78 ''ask'':114 ''better'':131 ''caleb'':75 ''come'':92 ''die'':48,50 ''etern'':54 ''faith'':10 ''fear'':7 ''gad'':99 ''generat'':64 ''go'':104 ''god'':51,81 ''gonna'':4,13 ''grandkid'':90 ''grow'':122 ''guess'':26,85 ''half'':101 ''hint'':33 ''increas'':21 ''instead'':8 ''isn'':65 ''joshua'':73 ''know'':71 ''land'':18 ''leav'':39 ''live'':77 ''manasseh'':103 ''mean'':56 ''men'':24 ''okay'':115 ''outsid'':15 ''parent'':127 ''pictur'':96 ''prepar'':67 ''promis'':17 ''re'':113 ''realli'':3,19 ''replac'':125 ''reuben'':97 ''sin'':23 ''stay'':14 ''still'':53,59 ''succumb'':5 ''wait'':60 ''wander'':46,47,49 ''want'':119 ''wilder'':43 ''yet'':37'::tsvector, '{"text":"Are you really gonna succumb to fear instead of faith? Are you gonna stay outside the promised land? Really? An increase of sinful men because guess what? And here''s what he hints at. He will yet again leave them in the wilderness. It''s wander, wander, die, wander, die. God is still eternal, which means he can still wait. And if this generation isn''t prepared, I don''t know if Joshua and Caleb can live another 40, but God can, and I guess it will be the grandkids that come in. Now you picture Reuben and Gad and half of Manasseh going, no, no, no. That''s not what we''re asking. Okay? We don''t want to just grow up and replace our parents and be no better than they were.","seq_end":5146,"t_end_s":20444.24,"seq_start":5135,"t_start_s":20399.406,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#5449', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''10'':62 ''abl'':94 ''actual'':97 ''balaam'':53 ''balak'':55 ''brazen'':18 ''chosen'':28,38 ''couldn'':2 ''easi'':12 ''faith'':66 ''fear'':59 ''final'':92 ''generat'':79,103 ''god'':25 ''greatest'':102 ''happen'':74 ''heed'':57 ''level'':84 ''levit'':31 ''look'':4 ''manna'':9 ''mose'':29 ''past'':5 ''potenti'':87 ''prophet'':91 ''rather'':63 ''realli'':26,99 ''rise'':78,81 ''say'':96 ''serpent'':19 ''simplic'':7 ''succumb'':46 ''temptat'':51 ''truli'':80 ''trust'':23 ''two'':69 ''want'':35 ''way'':15,44 ''wouldn'':21 ''wrong'':43'::tsvector, '{"text":"They couldn''t look past the simplicity of manna or the easiness of the way with that brazen serpent. They wouldn''t trust that God really had chosen Moses and Levites. No, they all wanted to be chosen themselves, but in the wrong way. They succumbed to some of the temptations of Balaam and Balak. They heeded the fear of the 10 rather than the faith of the two. And this is what happened. When will a rising generation truly rise to the level of their potential? When will a prophet finally be able to say, actually, this really is the greatest generation?","seq_end":5462,"t_end_s":21663.906,"seq_start":5449,"t_start_s":21620.219,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#5486', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''ago'':74 ''area'':6 ''begin'':76 ''book'':58 ''certain'':67 ''chanc'':31 ''close'':87 ''d'':27 ''die'':64,123 ''divin'':135 ''elder'':117 ''faith'':131 ''fellow'':116 ''felt'':44 ''find'':16 ''go'':91 ''goal'':68 ''god'':143 ''heart'':149 ''home'':92 ''island'':36 ''keep'':139 ''kind'':48,110 ''knew'':25 ''land'':104 ''last'':5,18,30 ''live'':99 ''m'':90 ''mind'':150,151 ''mission'':41,79,83 ''month'':95 ''number'':60 ''one'':17 ''principl'':112 ''promis'':103,136 ''right'':1 ''say'':21 ''see'':101 ''sent'':10 ''set'':70 ''sister'':119 ''soul'':19 ''strength'':153 ''strong'':46 ''taught'':108,114 ''teach'':33,38,54,145 ''thing'':50 ''today'':55 ''tri'':14 ''trust'':134 ''two'':72 ''us'':127 ''ve'':52 ''wander'':62,63,121,122 ''wanna'':98 ''want'':126 ''whole'':35,40 ''word'':141 ''year'':73'::tsvector, '{"text":"Right before my that last area where I was sent off to to try to find one last soul to say. And it I knew it''d be my last chance to teach the whole island, to teach the whole mission. And I felt so strongly the kinds of things I''ve been teaching today from the book of numbers about wander, wander, die. There are certain goals I set from two years ago, the beginning of my mission, and as a mission, we are this close. But I''m going home in a month, and I wanna live to see the promised land. And I just taught these kinds of principles. I taught my fellow elders and sisters about wander, wander, die. I I wanted us to to have faith and to trust divine promises and to keep the word of God and teach with all our heart, mind, mind, and strength.","seq_end":5500,"t_end_s":21787.842,"seq_start":5486,"t_start_s":21732.52,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#0', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''ahead'':103 ''back'':56 ''believ'':16 ''better'':86,89 ''come'':104 ''cometh'':6 ''confront'':36 ''could'':47 ''cover'':67 ''david'':78 ''declar'':45 ''deep'':26 ''destroy'':42 ''earth'':13 ''elah'':99 ''even'':85 ''faith'':10,44 ''find'':9 ''first'':72 ''friend'':53 ''giant'':102 ''halverson'':62 ''hello'':51 ''help'':17 ''jacob'':33 ''jare'':61 ''know'':77,83 ''lord'':14 ''m'':60 ''man'':5 ''may'':21 ''mine'':19 ''one'':38 ''place'':90 ''rest'':70 ''samuel'':73 ''shaken'':50 ''shall'':7 ''son'':3 ''sought'':40 ''strong'':29 ''testimoni'':23 ''thou'':18 ''today'':64 ''unbelief'':20 ''unshaken'':58 ''valley'':97 ''wanna'':82 ''welcom'':55 ''well'':74'::tsvector, '{"text":"When the son of man cometh, shall he find faith in the earth? Lord, I believe. Help thou mine unbelief. May our testimonies be as deep and as strong as that of Jacob, who, when confronted by one who sought to destroy his faith, declared, I could not be shaken. Hello, my friends, and welcome back to Unshaken. I''m Jared Halverson, and today we are covering all the rest of first Samuel. Well, now we know David, and I just wanna know him even better, and no better place to do it than in the Valley Of Elah with a giant ahead of him.","seq_end":11,"t_end_s":54.195,"seq_start":0,"t_start_s":0.72,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#131', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''armi'':59 ''armor'':17 ''ask'':65 ''battl'':51 ''beat'':90 ''behind'':33 ''better'':21 ''call'':56 ''day'':63 ''death'':85 ''els'':4,35 ''everi'':62 ''faith'':14,37 ''fight'':71,82 ''god'':19 ''goliath'':55 ''gonna'':76,99 ''heat'':49 ''hide'':32 ''hold'':23 ''israel'':61 ''israelit'':92 ''keep'':53 ''let'':1 ''like'':94,95 ''m'':97 ''might'':39 ''philistin'':89 ''protect'':7 ''re'':29 ''read'':54 ''send'':67 ''shield'':12 ''somebodi'':34,69 ''someon'':3 ''suffici'':41 ''take'':80 ''talk'':9 ''time'':44 ''tri'':30 ''trust'':2 ''well'':52 ''win'':88,100 ''winner'':79 ''within'':47'::tsvector, '{"text":"Let trust someone else with your protection. We talk about the shield of faith in the armor of God. You better be holding your own because if you''re trying to hide behind somebody else''s faith, that might be sufficient for a time, but not within the heat of battle. Well, keep reading. Goliath calls out the armies of Israel every day. He asks them, send me somebody to fight with, and it''s gonna be a winner take all fight to the death. If I win, Philistines beat the Israelites, and like like I''m not gonna win.","seq_end":138,"t_end_s":602.42,"seq_start":131,"t_start_s":567.725,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#304', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''36'':74 ''advantag'':57 ''armi'':105 ''base'':12 ''bear'':32,83 ''beat'':29 ''credenti'':6 ''david'':14,66 ''defi'':103 ''develop'':48 ''dig'':92 ''experi'':16,28 ''face'':20 ''faith'':46 ''give'':35 ''god'':33,109 ''goliath'':21 ''hath'':102 ''hope'':23,54 ''impress'':5 ''lion'':30,80 ''live'':108 ''next'':73 ''notic'':69 ''one'':97 ''opportun'':37,60 ''pass'':62 ''philistin'':87 ''preliminari'':64 ''prior'':27 ''reflex'':51 ''religi'':91 ''righteous'':50 ''say'':11,72 ''see'':100 ''servant'':76 ''shall'':94 ''simpli'':10 ''slew'':77 ''spiritu'':41 ''strength'':42 ''take'':56 ''test'':39,65 ''thi'':75 ''tri'':44 ''uncircumcis'':86 ''us'':36 ''would'':9'::tsvector, '{"text":"Now those are some impressive credentials. And I would simply say based on David''s experience that before we face Goliath, I hope we have some prior experience beating lions and bears. God will give us opportunities to test our spiritual strength, to try our faith, to develop some righteous reflexes. I just hope we take advantage of those opportunities and pass those preliminary tests. David did. But notice what he says next, 36. Thy servant slew both the lion and the bear, and this uncircumcised Philistine, there''s the religious dig again, shall be as one of them, seeing he hath defied the armies of the living God.","seq_end":317,"t_end_s":1374.315,"seq_start":304,"t_start_s":1326.465,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#338', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''absenc'':114 ''armor'':46,58,65 ''attack'':106 ''complet'':113 ''coupl'':10 ''david'':2 ''enemi'':25,28 ''fair'':73,89 ''faith'':108,116 ''fight'':23,74,90 ''flesh'':48,67 ''go'':53 ''god'':60,80 ''goliath'':19 ''lesson'':11 ''level'':38 ''lower'':34 ''m'':32,52 ''never'':86 ''oh'':78 ''one'':13 ''peopl'':105 ''posit'':111 ''put'':3 ''see'':101 ''settl'':62 ''side'':83 ''similar'':17 ''sometim'':103 ''take'':55 ''think'':50 ''trust'':97 ''uh'':76,77 ''uh-uh'':75 ''weapon'':30 ''would'':21,85'::tsvector, '{"text":"And David put them off him. There''s a couple lessons there. One, again, this this similarity to Goliath. Why would I fight the enemy with the enemy''s weapons? I''m just lowering myself to their level. And if all they have is the armor of flesh, you think I''m going to take off the armor of God and settle for the armor of flesh just so it''s a fair fight? Uh-uh. Oh, with God on my side, it would never be a fair fight nor should it be, and I trust in him. I see that sometimes when people attack the faith from a position of complete absence of faith.","seq_end":348,"t_end_s":1518.175,"seq_start":338,"t_start_s":1477.1,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#547', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''across'':54 ''action'':82 ''approach'':28 ''armi'':43,62 ''aros'':44 ''begin'':35 ''boy'':101 ''came'':49,52 ''chapter'':4 ''close'':8 ''come'':5 ''complet'':63 ''confid'':64 ''faith'':93,97 ''fear'':91 ''fell'':40 ''get'':77 ''god'':66 ''goliath'':39 ''happen'':22 ''inact'':80 ''israelit'':42 ''know'':20 ''later'':12 ''littl'':100 ''move'':88 ''one'':99 ''philistin'':61 ''rout'':16 ''rush'':53 ''take'':26,58,75,86 ''talk'':32 ''took'':95 ''valley'':56 ''vers'':11 ''went'':46 ''winner'':25 ''would'':67'::tsvector, '{"text":"And as the chapter comes to its close a few verses later, it''s a rout. I don''t know what happened to the winner takes all approach that they had talked about to begin with, but once Goliath fell, the Israelite army arose. He went down, they came up, and came rushing across the valley to take on the Philistine army, completely confident that God would be with them too. What did it take to get them from inaction to action? What did it take to move them from fear to faith? It took the faith of one little boy.","seq_end":556,"t_end_s":2350.965,"seq_start":547,"t_start_s":2314.575,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#786', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''bulli'':7 ''certain'':10 ''complaint'':17 ''daughter'':2 ''david'':115 ''deris'':21 ''everyth'':84 ''face'':26 ''faith'':66 ''fallen'':112 ''feel'':108 ''fell'':99 ''goe'':74,82 ''gonna'':79 ''good'':58 ''life'':14 ''molli'':32 ''mormon'':33 ''peopl'':18,40 ''person'':46 ''pure'':70 ''righteous'':68 ''said'':3,19 ''saul'':85 ''say'':80 ''short'':100,113 ''speak'':36 ''stand'':86,94 ''standard'':117 ''target'':50 ''threw'':23 ''throw'':41 ''time'':11 ''tri'':55,63 ''use'':92 ''well'':76 ''wrong'':53,61 ''yet'':72'::tsvector, '{"text":"My daughter said that she was bullied at a certain time of her life, and the complaint people said, the derision they threw in her face was that she was a molly Mormon. And that speaks more of the people throwing that out than the person that''s being targeted. What''s wrong with trying to be good? What''s wrong with trying to be faithful and righteous and pure? And yet that goes against well, I was gonna say it goes against everything Saul stands for. No. It''s all used to stand for it, but he fell short of it, and that''s why he feels that he''s fallen short of David''s standard.","seq_end":795,"t_end_s":3372.315,"seq_start":786,"t_start_s":3331.76,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#1276', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''14'':44 ''accus'':38 ''ahimelech'':23,45 ''among'':57 ''answer'':46 ''assum'':93 ''bid'':76 ''bring'':30 ''call'':21 ''david'':5,62,95 ''done'':36 ''ear'':7 ''end'':19 ''ever'':92 ''except'':103 ''faith'':56 ''fellow'':28 ''go'':106 ''goeth'':73 ''honor'':79 ''hous'':82 ''king'':48,66,105 ''law'':71 ''music'':3 ''nobodi'':100 ''priest'':29 ''protest'':85 ''said'':50 ''saul'':15 ''say'':32,87 ''servant'':60 ''son'':69 ''son-in-law'':68 ''song'':13 ''sour'':12 ''thi'':59,75 ''thine'':81 ''think'':101 ''treason'':41 ''turn'':97 ''vers'':43 ''wait'':51,88 ''woah'':52 ''would'':90'::tsvector, '{"text":"That''s music to David''s ears, but that''s a sour song for Saul. And so he ends up calling for Ahimelech and all of his fellow priests, brings them, says, what have you done? He accuses them of treason. And verse 14, Ahimelech answered the king and said, wait. Woah. Who is so faithful among all thy servants as David, which is the king''s son-in-law, and goeth at thy bidding and is honorable in thine house? He''s protesting and saying, wait, why would I ever assume that David is turned against you? Nobody thinks that except you, king.","seq_end":1285,"t_end_s":5458.25,"seq_start":1276,"t_start_s":5421.95,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#1286', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''ago'':111 ''allianc'':66 ''anyth'':26 ''ask'':28 ''conclus'':59 ''cri'':15 ''fact'':53,88 ''faith'':5 ''fall'':115 ''guy'':20 ''honor'':19 ''jump'':55 ''kill'':73,85,91 ''know'':22 ''law'':13 ''ll'':24,90 ''loud'':17 ''loyal'':33 ''moment'':110 ''nob'':96 ''one'':2,30 ''opposit'':58 ''priest'':94 ''re'':77 ''saul'':49,54 ''say'':61,114 ''scare'':105 ''serv'':36,42 ''servant'':102 ''side'':80 ''sinc'':70 ''slaughter'':118 ''son'':11 ''son-in-law'':10 ''spear'':108 ''take'':50 ''thought'':39 ''turn'':99 ''upon'':116 ''wanna'':72 ''well'':44'::tsvector, '{"text":"No one''s more faithful. He''s your own son-in-law for crying out loud. Most honorable guy I know. He''ll do anything you ask. No one is more loyal. So by serving him, I thought I was serving you. Well, that''s not how Saul takes it. In fact, Saul jumps to the opposite conclusion and says, no. You are in alliance with him. And since I wanna kill him and you''re on his side, I am here to kill you. In fact, I''ll kill all the priests of Nob. And he turns to his servants that were scared of his spear a moment ago, and they say, fall upon them. Slaughter them all.","seq_end":1293,"t_end_s":5495.975,"seq_start":1286,"t_start_s":5459.375,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#1574', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''abigail'':91,98,119 ''ad'':52 ''assign'':55 ''caleb'':2 ''caus'':100 ''charact'':58 ''coven'':11 ''cute'':76 ''doubt'':65 ''either'':111 ''exampl'':37 ''fact'':31 ''faith'':14 ''father'':104,109 ''fool'':62,78 ''fortun'':97 ''get'':25 ''give'':3,18 ''joy'':102,106,117 ''keep'':9,12 ''later'':53 ''let'':79 ''littl'':77 ''live'':86 ''ll'':8,122 ''look'':73 ''lot'':115 ''mean'':61,68,99 ''moment'':127 ''mother'':69 ''mountain'':6,21 ''must'':49 ''name'':47,81,90 ''nebal'':15,29,60,84 ''oh'':1,72 ''one'':34 ''real'':46 ''rejoic'':110 ''rich'':26 ''say'':71 ''see'':123 ''type'':59 ''unfortun'':85 ''wanna'':24 ''way'':42,112 ''well'':67 ''would'':70'::tsvector, '{"text":"Oh, Caleb, give me this mountain. I''ll keep the covenant, keep the faith. Nebal was more, give me this mountain because I wanna get rich on it. Nebal, in fact this is one of those examples that there''s no way that was his real name. This must have been added later to assign him his character type. Nebal means fool, and I doubt any well meaning mother would say, oh, look at this cute little fool. Let''s name him that. Nebal, unfortunately, lived up to his name. Abigail did too, but that''s fortunate. Abigail means cause of joy or father''s joy or my father rejoices. Either way, there''s lot of joy in Abigail, and we''ll see why in a moment.","seq_end":1579,"t_end_s":6670.025,"seq_start":1574,"t_start_s":6632.36,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#2130', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''along'':63 ''come'':31,83,109 ''david'':37 ''day'':106,114 ''evil'':101 ''faith'':60 ''fellow'':28 ''found'':100 ''gain'':59 ''gath'':22 ''go'':79 ''god'':53 ''good'':3,92 ''hast'':74 ''host'':90 ''invok'':51 ''israel'':55 ''jesus'':1 ''king'':20 ''know'':7 ''live'':115,116 ''liveth'':47,72 ''lord'':46,71 ''meantim'':68 ''philistin'':29 ''relent'':23 ''say'':35 ''seven'':42 ''sight'':95 ''sinc'':104 ''six'':40 ''still'':18 ''sure'':43 ''thee'':103 ''thi'':78,82,108 ''thou'':73 ''understand'':25 ''unto'':110,112 ''upright'':76 ''vers'':39 ''way'':17 ''wow'':48'::tsvector, '{"text":"Jesus is good. I don''t know what you have against him. Can we be that way? Still, the king of Gath relents. He understands where his fellow Philistines are coming from, and he says to David in verse six and seven, surely as the Lord liveth. Wow. He''s invoking the God of Israel now as he gained faith in him along the or in the meantime. As the Lord liveth, thou hast been upright, and thy going out and thy coming in with me in in the host is good in my sight. For I have not found evil in thee since the day of thy coming unto me unto this day.","seq_end":2137,"t_end_s":9117.251,"seq_start":2130,"t_start_s":9081.949,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#2138', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''actual'':60 ''anoth'':95 ''ask'':104 ''away'':31 ''best'':74 ''birth'':93 ''child'':96,112 ''close'':100 ''come'':38 ''convict'':81 ''could'':54,77 ''deep'':80 ''displeas'':17 ''experi'':63 ''faith'':82 ''favor'':5 ''gave'':92 ''go'':12 ''godpar'':109 ''gold'':73 ''heart'':46 ''imagin'':78 ''isn'':47 ''know'':43 ''lord'':3,20,85 ''lutheran'':79 ''neighbor'':66 ''nevertheless'':1 ''pain'':26 ''peac'':14 ''peopl'':75,88 ''philistin'':23 ''pleas'':42 ''re'':37 ''realli'':25 ''return'':10 ''see'':34 ''send'':29 ''solid'':72 ''stay'':55 ''tennesse'':68 ''thee'':6 ''thou'':16 ''wherefor'':8 ''wife'':57 ''wish'':52 ''wonder'':86,87 ''would'':105'::tsvector, '{"text":"Nevertheless, the Lord''s favor thee not. Wherefore now return and go in peace, that thou displease not the Lords of the Philistine. It really pains me to send you away, but I see where they''re coming from, and just please know that my heart isn''t in this. I wish you could stay. My wife and I actually had this experience with our neighbors in Tennessee that were just solid gold, best people you could imagine. Lutherans, deep conviction, faith in the Lord, wonderful, wonderful people. And when they gave birth to another child, we were so close to them, they asked, would you be the godparents of our child?","seq_end":2143,"t_end_s":9156.195,"seq_start":2138,"t_start_s":9117.811,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#2204', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''200'':109 ''600'':70,112 ''absolut'':115 ''answer'':36 ''arm'':71 ''back'':83 ''brook'':108 ''david'':8,18,39,68 ''direct'':44 ''divin'':43 ''eight'':17 ''ephod'':15 ''eventu'':85 ''exhaust'':116 ''fail'':54 ''faith'':64 ''fals'':4 ''fill'':62 ''gather'':69,80 ''get'':95,102 ''go'':121 ''god'':35 ''goe'':74 ''guess'':90 ''inquir'':19 ''keep'':120 ''long'':92 ''lord'':22 ''men'':72,113 ''one'':105 ''overtak'':32,50 ''peopl'':82 ''promis'':60,67 ''propheci'':5,12 ''pursu'':26,45 ''raid'':78 ''recov'':55 ''river'':106 ''say'':23 ''seek'':10 ''shall'':24,30 ''shalt'':48 ''sure'':49 ''talk'':57 ''thou'':47 ''time'':100 ''trip'':93 ''troop'':29 ''true'':11 ''vers'':16 ''went'':2 ''without'':53 ''worthi'':41'::tsvector, '{"text":"He went to false prophecy, and now David is seeking true prophecy through the Ephod. Verse eight, David inquired at the Lord saying, shall I pursue after this troop? Shall I overtake them? And God answered him, so David is worthy of divine direction. Pursue, for thou shalt surely overtake them and without fail recover all. Talk about a promise. And filled with faith in that promise, David gathers 600 armed men and goes out in this raid to gather his people back. Now eventually, it''s a I guess a long trip to get there, and by the time they get to this one river, this brook, 200 of his 600 men are absolutely exhausted and can''t keep going.","seq_end":2212,"t_end_s":9459.12,"seq_start":2204,"t_start_s":9416.895,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#3262', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''actual'':28 ''advic'':73 ''appoint'':103 ''ark'':82 ''best'':32,72 ''contrari'':7 ''counsel'':65 ''counselor'':52 ''coven'':44 ''doctrin'':42 ''faith'':63 ''find'':19 ''first'':55 ''give'':69 ''go'':14 ''goldilock'':10 ''isn'':76 ''last'':38 ''like'':3,61 ''offic'':97 ''one'':29 ''part'':91 ''place'':33 ''presid'':56 ''proactiv'':22 ''re'':13 ''revel'':49 ''say'':59 ''second'':90 ''see'':35 ''speak'':24,67 ''stand'':94 ''steadi'':79 ''thing'':60 ''think'':27 ''tri'':17 ''ve'':101 ''well'':83 ''woah'':74 ''year'':39 ''zone'':11'::tsvector, '{"text":"It''s like there''s a contrary here, a Goldilocks zone we''re going have to try to find of being proactive and speaking up. I think actually one of the best places to see it is last year in the Doctrine and Covenants when we have the revelations to the counselors in the first presidency. When it says things like, be faithful in counsel, so speak up, give your very best advice. Woah, but isn''t that steady in the ark? Well, no, not if you do the second part, which is stand in the office to which you''ve been appointed.","seq_end":3269,"t_end_s":14055.3,"seq_start":3262,"t_start_s":14026.524,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#3570', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''alreadi'':12,21 ''ask'':132 ''concern'':105 ''day'':60,88 ''defeat'':92 ''faith'':103 ''far'':101 ''get'':30 ''glori'':75 ''goal'':118 ''gonna'':64 ''good'':6,115,124 ''guid'':54 ''help'':53 ''histori'':27 ''hold'':107 ''hundr'':40 ''idea'':125 ''john'':16 ''know'':9 ''last'':59,87 ''let'':110 ''littl'':71 ''m'':130 ''might'':91 ''mind'':98 ''mix'':32 ''nephi'':1 ''okay'':61,99 ''peopl'':56 ''plain'':77,84 ''propheci'':28 ''purpos'':94 ''re'':69 ''reveal'':13 ''revel'':18 ''rich'':66 ''righteous'':120 ''six'':39 ''somebodi'':111 ''sorri'':26 ''straightforward'':73 ''stuff'':7 ''symbol'':67 ''thing'':116 ''version'':48 ''wanna'':81 ''want'':51 ''write'':36 ''wrote'':22 ''year'':41'::tsvector, '{"text":"Nephi, what? This is the good stuff. I know. And I already revealed it to John the revelator, and he already wrote it down, or sorry, history, prophecy, I get them mixed up. He will write it down six hundred years from now. And that''s the version that I want to help guide the people through the last days. Okay? It''s gonna be richly symbolic. You''re a little too straightforward. You glory in plainness. I don''t wanna be that plain about the last days because it might defeat some purposes I have in mind. Okay? As far as faith is concerned. So hold off and let somebody it''s a good thing. Your goal was righteous. You had a good idea. It''s just I''m not asking you to do it.","seq_end":3576,"t_end_s":15427.806,"seq_start":3570,"t_start_s":15388.13,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#3577', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''author'':68,74 ''beauti'':112 ''build'':49 ''choic'':29 ''church'':117 ''credit'':91 ''day'':120 ''deleg'':36 ''deserv'':89 ''didn'':132 ''els'':4 ''enough'':87 ''everyon'':64 ''exampl'':142 ''except'':65 ''faith'':79 ''far'':31 ''finish'':76 ''god'':55,71 ''hinckley'':150 ''honor'':10,16,25 ''joseph'':124 ''kingdom'':53 ''long'':59,86 ''lord'':12,18,27 ''lorenzo'':144 ''mean'':70 ''okay'':92 ''one'':83 ''origin'':67 ''outliv'':63 ''portion'':38 ''present'':85 ''presid'':114,149 ''process'':60 ''rest'':94 ''said'':44 ''see'':110 ''smith'':125 ''snow'':145 ''someon'':3 ''sometim'':9,22 ''take'':98 ''thing'':122,129,147 ''think'':108 ''time'':20 ''turn'':103 ''two'':105 ''us'':96 ''ve'':43 ''wait'':137 ''want'':2 ''wheel'':100 ''wilford'':139 ''woodruff'':140'::tsvector, '{"text":"I want someone else to do it. And sometimes honoring the Lord''s will is honoring the Lord''s timing. And sometimes it''s honoring the Lord''s choice as far as who is he delegating what portion of it to. I''ve said this before that the building up of the kingdom of God is such a long process that it outlives everyone except its original author, which means God, is the author and finisher of our faith, is the only one there present long enough to deserve the credit. Okay? The rest of us only take the wheel for a turn or two. And I think we see that beautifully in presidents of the church in our day, and things that Joseph Smith did, but other things that he didn''t do, and that waited for Wilford Woodruff, for example, or Lorenzo Snow, or things that President Hinckley","seq_end":3588,"t_end_s":15480.385,"seq_start":3577,"t_start_s":15428.365,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#3836', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''actual'':37 ''aren'':122 ''back'':85 ''believ'':89 ''better'':117 ''bless'':62,87 ''build'':2,52 ''christian'':130,132 ''church'':99 ''come'':84 ''contribut'':80 ''cours'':68 ''david'':43 ''dedic'':48 ''denomin'':128 ''dwell'':13 ''end'':60 ''entir'':64 ''faith'':138,143 ''flavor'':141 ''god'':56 ''gonna'':59,83 ''good'':135 ''help'':32 ''high'':11 ''hous'':4 ''invit'':28,72 ''kingdom'':54,105 ''love'':40 ''m'':47 ''make'':78 ''member'':96 ''might'':144 ''name'':7 ''nation'':109 ''non'':131 ''part'':125 ''particip'':76 ''peopl'':136 ''re'':19,27 ''religion'':119,133 ''see'':102 ''surround'':104 ''therein'':14 ''thing'':50 ''tri'':20 ''us'':33 ''want'':70 ''whatev'':140 ''whether'':106,114 ''within'':129 ''world'':30,65,74 ''yet'':118'::tsvector, '{"text":"To build a house to my name for the most high to dwell therein. That''s what we''re trying to do. That''s what we''re inviting the world to help us with. That''s actually what I love about what David is doing. I''m dedicating these things to build the kingdom of God. That''s gonna end up blessing the entire world. So, of course, I want to invite the world to participate, to make a contribution. It''s gonna come back to bless you, believe me. Can we do that as members of the church? Do we see the surrounding kingdoms, whether those are nations other than our own, whether those are better yet, religions that we aren''t a part of, other denominations within Christianity, non Christian religions, just good people of faith of whatever flavor that faith might be,","seq_end":3850,"t_end_s":16702.217,"seq_start":3836,"t_start_s":16649.125,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940#3865', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 17 - 2 Samuel 10 - David: From Shepherd to King', '''alway'':44 ''christ'':105 ''church'':35 ''cours'':26 ''custodian'':79 ''day'':19 ''dispens'':65,83,92 ''ephesian'':62 ''f'':2 ''faith'':37 ''final'':82 ''full'':68 ''gather'':99 ''go'':29 ''god'':27 ''invit'':54 ''job'':88,94 ''kind'':33 ''latter'':18 ''love'':61 ''much'':8 ''one'':63,101 ''open'':52 ''orson'':1 ''particip'':56 ''peopl'':39 ''said'':4 ''saint'':20 ''thing'':103 ''time'':70 ''us'':48 ''use'':31 ''whitney'':3 ''work'':9 ''world'':14'::tsvector, '{"text":"Orson F. Whitney said there''s too much work to do on the world for just the Latter day Saints to do it. So of course, God''s going to use all kinds of churches and faiths and peoples. And he does. He always has. And for us to have the openness to invite their participation. That''s why I love Ephesians one. The dispensation of the fullness of times, that''s ours. And if we are the custodians of this final dispensation, then what''s our job? It''s this dispensation''s job, which is what? To gather in one all things in Christ.","seq_end":3878,"t_end_s":16785.465,"seq_start":3865,"t_start_s":16747.25,"episode_id":"unshaken-O3SiM9Yi940"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-RLirbnj-kGk#0', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Kings 12-22 - Elijah''s Ministry and Miracles', '''advantag'':116 ''alway'':138 ''back'':55 ''believ'':16 ''come'':153 ''cometh'':6 ''confront'':36 ''could'':47 ''cover'':92 ''declar'':45 ''deep'':26 ''destroy'':42 ''earth'':13 ''face'':146,148 ''faith'':10,44 ''find'':9 ''friend'':53 ''half'':104 ''halverson'':61 ''hello'':51 ''help'':17 ''hope'':65,112 ''hour'':105 ''jacob'':33 ''jare'':60 ''know'':124 ''last'':71,84 ''lord'':14 ''m'':59 ''man'':5,149 ''marathon'':76,82,90 ''materi'':95 ''may'':21 ''met'':132 ''mine'':19 ''much'':94 ''one'':38 ''person'':135 ''re'':144 ''realli'':64,111 ''recov'':69 ''say'':139 ''seven'':101 ''shaken'':50 ''shall'':7 ''slow'':152 ''someon'':133 ''son'':3 ''sought'':40 ''sound'':151 ''speak'':145 ''speed'':120 ''strong'':29 ''technolog'':118 ''testimoni'':23 ''thing'':122 ''thou'':18 ''took'':99,115 ''ultra'':81,88,89 ''unbelief'':20 ''unshaken'':57 ''us'':100 ''ve'':131 ''week'':72,85 ''welcom'':54 ''yeah'':140'::tsvector, '{"text":"When the son of man cometh, shall he find faith in the earth? Lord, I believe. Help thou mine unbelief. May our testimonies be as deep and as strong as that of Jacob, who, when confronted by one who sought to destroy his faith, declared, I could not be shaken. Hello, my friends. Welcome back to Unshaken. I''m Jared Halverson, and I really hope that you have recovered from last week. Now there are marathons, and then there are ultra marathons, and last week was an ultra ultra marathon. We covered so much material, and it only took us seven and a half hours to do it. So I really hope that you took advantage of technology to speed up things. I know some of you do that. I''ve met someone in person, and they always say, yeah. When when we''re speaking face to face, man, you sound slow","seq_end":12,"t_end_s":67.72,"seq_start":0,"t_start_s":0.72,"episode_id":"unshaken-RLirbnj-kGk"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-RLirbnj-kGk#83', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Kings 12-22 - Elijah''s Ministry and Miracles', '''ask'':56 ''bigger'':74,76 ''cri'':10 ''dilig'':39 ''effort'':18 ''enrich'':31 ''faith'':40 ''good'':53 ''humbl'':41 ''kind'':86 ''kingdom'':33 ''lead'':99 ''leader'':89 ''left'':29 ''lighten'':4 ''ll'':59 ''load'':6 ''loud'':12 ''lower'':7 ''mean'':26 ''moment'':67 ''much'':17 ''name'':84 ''project'':24 ''public'':22 ''question'':77 ''rehoboth'':61,83 ''reign'':44 ''requir'':15 ''respons'':63 ''see'':60 ''serv'':37 ''strength'':101 ''tax'':8 ''term'':20 ''thing'':54 ''think'':70 ''throughout'':42 ''type'':97 ''weak'':103 ''well'':46 ''work'':23'::tsvector, '{"text":"If you will lighten that load, lower taxes for crying out loud. Don''t require so much effort in terms of public works projects. I mean, what''s left? He enriched the kingdom. Then we will serve you diligently, faithfully, humbly throughout your reign as well. Now that''s that was a good thing to ask, and we''ll see Rehoboth''s response in just a moment, but I think there''s a bigger a bigger question here, and it''s for Rehoboth. Namely, what kind of a leader will you be? Will you be the type that leads in strength or weakness?","seq_end":93,"t_end_s":501.015,"seq_start":83,"t_start_s":464.835,"episode_id":"unshaken-RLirbnj-kGk"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-RLirbnj-kGk#487', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Kings 12-22 - Elijah''s Ministry and Miracles', '''actual'':47 ''attack'':4 ''bet'':55 ''book'':6 ''came'':104 ''didn'':16,58 ''doesn'':30 ''dupe'':81 ''enough'':22 ''faith'':76 ''gather'':106 ''geographi'':20 ''greater'':99 ''inherit'':36 ''israel'':102 ''ite'':27 ''jeroboam'':90 ''jerusalem'':29,108 ''joseph'':14,56 ''know'':18,33,60,67 ''least'':87 ''left'':101 ''like'':9,70 ''manasseh'':26,41 ''mormon'':8 ''north'':44 ''offer'':92 ''oh'':12,45 ''path'':85,97 ''peopl'':2 ''probabl'':52 ''put'':24 ''re'':49,51 ''resist'':88,100 ''right'':53 ''say'':11 ''see'':13 ''smith'':15,57 ''took'':95 ''tribe'':39,114 ''vers'':69 ''well'':21 ''weren'':79'::tsvector, '{"text":"And people that attack the Book of Mormon like to say, oh, see? Joseph Smith didn''t know his geography well enough. He put a Manasseh ite in Jerusalem. Doesn''t he know that the inheritance of the tribe of Manasseh was further north? Oh, he actually, you''re they''re probably right. I bet Joseph Smith didn''t know that. But what they don''t know is verses like this that those who were faithful, those that weren''t duped by the the path of least resistance that Jeroboam was offering them, They took the path of greater resistance, left Israel, and came and gathered to Jerusalem themselves from all these other tribes.","seq_end":496,"t_end_s":2253.655,"seq_start":487,"t_start_s":2214.245,"episode_id":"unshaken-RLirbnj-kGk"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-RLirbnj-kGk#497', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Kings 12-22 - Elijah''s Ministry and Miracles', '''abl'':100 ''actual'':46 ''ancestri'':53 ''becom'':20 ''burn'':39 ''chronicl'':5 ''day'':110 ''decid'':64 ''divers'':23 ''faith'':38 ''fire'':36 ''found'':98 ''go'':18,83 ''gonna'':72 ''grandpa'':57,59 ''great'':58 ''high'':49 ''includ'':14 ''increas'':22 ''inherit'':81 ''israel'':13 ''jerusalem'':16 ''land'':78,88 ''leav'':76 ''lehi'':51,97 ''manasseh'':15 ''melt'':24,31 ''pick'':73 ''pot'':25 ''power'':112 ''promis'':90 ''re'':29,71 ''realli'':48 ''said'':6 ''solomon'':44 ''speak'':47 ''specif'':87 ''templ'':42,66,93 ''tribe'':11 ''well'':54 ''whoever'':55,60 ''wonder'':96 ''worth'':68'::tsvector, '{"text":"That''s what the chronicler said out of all the tribes of Israel, including Manasseh. Jerusalem is going to become an increasingly diverse melting pot, and what they''re all melting into is the the fire of faith burning from the Temple Of Solomon. This actually speaks really highly of Lehi''s ancestry. Well, whoever is grandpa, great grandpa, whoever it was that decided the temple''s worth it. We''re gonna pick up and leave the land of our inheritance and go to a more specific land of promise where the temple is. No wonder Lehi found himself able to do that all over again in his own day. So powerful.","seq_end":510,"t_end_s":2298.29,"seq_start":497,"t_start_s":2253.895,"episode_id":"unshaken-RLirbnj-kGk"}'::jsonb)
